From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:58:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Count a chord with half its heads dotted as dotted

AbstractChordInter.countDots takes the mean of its heads' dot counts and
rounds it with Math.rint, so a chord dotted on exactly half its heads
(one of two, two of four) gets no dot and the dot it has is removed.
With the dots of a chord checked top down (the previous patch), the
owner's nine songs have seven such chords, all dotted in print, each
missing a dot for another reason: two dots on either side of a ledger
glued into one glyph (Piano Man 191, 192), a dot printed a space above
the low note of an octave below three ledgers or never a symbol
candidate (Piano Man 100, 202), a dot below the staff read by OCR as a
lyric letter (Yellow Submarine 3, 4). A printed dot is lost far more
often than one is made up, and the heads of a chord share one duration:
the half now rounds up (Math.floor(mean + 0.5)).

On the nine songs this changes exactly those seven chords, all as
printed, and nothing else.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETLv1P36qBemBoAsvF94d2
---
 .../org/audiveris/omr/sig/inter/AbstractChordInter.java    | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/org/audiveris/omr/sig/inter/AbstractChordInter.java b/app/src/main/java/org/audiveris/omr/sig/inter/AbstractChordInter.java
index b4a29a3ec..28d13dae6 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/org/audiveris/omr/sig/inter/AbstractChordInter.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/org/audiveris/omr/sig/inter/AbstractChordInter.java
@@ -284,7 +284,12 @@ public abstract class AbstractChordInter
 
             double val = pop.getMeanValue();
             double std = pop.getStandardDeviation();
-            dotsNumber = (int) Math.rint(val);
+
+            // Half the heads dotted counts as dotted (rint rounded 0.5 down): a printed dot is
+            // lost far more often than one is made up (two dots glued across a ledger into one
+            // glyph, a dot read as a lyric letter, a dot printed beyond reach of its head), and
+            // the heads of a chord share one duration.
+            dotsNumber = (int) Math.floor(val + 0.5);
 
             if (std != 0) {
                 logger.debug("Inconsistent dots in {}, assumed {}", this, dotsNumber);
